# Files exempt from tools/check-no-site-data.sh.
#
# Keep this list short and justify every entry. Exempting a file is in the
# same category as pushing with --no-verify: it is sometimes correct, and it
# is always worth a second pair of eyes. Everything listed here is read by
# nobody's scanner, so a real leak added to one of these files ships.
#
# One glob per line, matched against the repo-relative path.

# Implementation plans quote the scanner's own test fixtures verbatim -- the
# sample hostnames, documentation-reserved addresses, and placeholder mount
# and home paths it is built to detect -- so they necessarily trip the scanner
# they describe. Every such value is invented or reserved for documentation.
# Exempting these is preferable to weakening the patterns, which would blind
# the scanner to the real thing.
#
# Note this file is deliberately NOT self-exempt: the exemption list is
# security-relevant, so it has to survive its own scan. Describe fixtures here
# rather than reproducing them.
docs/superpowers/plans/*.md
